## Instructions

1. Read the document text carefully.
2. Classify by document FORMAT, not by the deal type it relates to.
3. A lease proposal in letter format is "Letter of Intent", not "Lease".
4. If no listed type clearly applies, do NOT default to "Other". Instead, put your own best
   specific label for what the document actually is (e.g. "Marketing Flyer", "Correspondence",
   "Permit") in "documentType" — a specific guess, even one outside this list, is far more
   useful for taxonomy review than a generic catch-all. Only use "Other" when you genuinely
   cannot describe what kind of document it is at all.
5. If your confidence is below 0.7, or "documentType" is a guess outside the list above,
   include up to 3 alternative types you considered in "candidates", each with its own
   confidence. Otherwise omit "candidates" or return an empty array.

## Output Format

Respond with a JSON object:

{
  "documentType": "<one of the types listed above, or your own specific label if none fit>",
  "confidence": <float 0.0-1.0>,
  "reasoning": "<1-2 sentence explanation>",
  "candidates": [
    { "documentType": "<an alternative type you considered>", "confidence": <float 0.0-1.0> }
  ]
}
